[size=5][b]Marriage Calculation Assistant[/b][/size]

[size=5][b]At a glance[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]🟢 [b]Version 3.0.1[/b] · Built for CK3 [b]1.19.x[/b]; tested on [b]1.19.0.6[/b].
[*]🟢 [b]Requires Parley: The Negotiating Table.[/b] Load MCA after Parley.
[*]🟢 [b]Candidate scores, hover breakdowns and optional score sorting[/b] in the marriage picker.
[*]🟢 [b]Nine languages:[/b] English, French, German, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Russian, Simplified Chinese and Spanish.
[*]🔴 [b]The score measures candidate gameplay potential.[/b] It is not AI marriage acceptance or a prediction of the outcome of a particular marriage.
[*]🔴 [b]Marriage-window conflict:[/b] another mod replacing [b]gui/interaction_marriage.gui[/b] needs a functional compatibility patch.
[*]🔴 [b]Multiplayer is unverified.[/b] Check the compatibility section before combining marriage-interface mods.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Find the person behind the list[/b][/size]

A useful claim, an exceptional mind or a powerful potential ally: the best candidate depends on what you need. Find promising names in a long marriage list, then hover their scores to see what makes them stand out.

[size=5][b]Compare candidates without losing the details[/b][/size]

MCA adds a score to candidate rows in CK3's marriage picker. Hover the number for a breakdown of its components. Switch to [b]MCA: by score[/b] to bring the highest-scoring candidates to the top.

It works when choosing a potential spouse from another court and when choosing someone from your own court to offer in marriage. Both lists use the same core components and weights. Potential alliance strength contributes when reported by the game's picker, and adapters can add opportunities specific to a setting.

The score helps compare opportunities. It does not change marriage acceptance or modify the chosen candidate. Two candidates' scores are not prices to add together, and MCA points are separate from Parley's treaty score.

[size=5][b]What the score includes[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Visible inheritable qualities:[/b] active inheritable traits receive positive or negative weights. The three positive intelligence, beauty and physique tiers are worth +10, +20 and +30; their negative counterparts subtract the same amounts. Other supported inheritable traits have their own weights. Hidden or recessive genetics are not inspected.
[*][b]Skills:[/b] up to 30 points, based on the five public skills and the standard assist-spouse contribution. Candidates younger than an effective age of 16, or incapable candidates, receive zero for this component. The score does not assume they will be eligible to serve on your council.
[*][b]Age-based reproductive potential:[/b] a 0–20 index using effective age and selected visible restrictions. It is not a birth probability. A child's zero here describes current potential, not a prediction of lifelong childlessness.
[*][b]Dynastic prestige potential:[/b] −5 to +45 points, scaled from the dynasty marriage-prestige table. This is an indication of dynastic standing, rather than the selected pair's exact prestige reward.
[*][b]Explicit claims:[/b] the strongest explicit claim contributes, up to 24 points; pressed claims receive twice the weight of unpressed claims of the same rank. Marriage does not immediately transfer a claim or title to you.
[*][b]Potential alliance:[/b] included only when the game's candidate row reports that opportunity, with up to 100 points based on the potential ally's military strength relative to yours. It does not guarantee military assistance.
[/list]

These components, plus any adapter contributions, add up to the displayed score. Their point values are design weights for comparing candidates, not percentages or amounts of a shared game resource. A strong total can therefore combine different advantages: inspect the breakdown to find the ones that matter to your plans.

Court position, arranger opinion and reluctance to release a courtier do not contribute. Hidden fertility/health, secret parentage, predicted children, the succession queue and the full utility of the selected couple are outside the model.

[size=5][b]How to use it[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Open a marriage picker and set the game's normal filters.
[*]Hover an [b]MCA[/b] number to inspect its components. The displayed breakdown adds up to the score.
[*]Close the filter panel and choose [b]MCA: by score[/b] for descending score order. Equal scores keep their current native order; unavailable scores go last.
[*]Choose [b]Default list[/b] to restore the native ordering and filter controls.
[/list]

The separate pinned-player row stays pinned. Changing the active picker side, marriage type or candidate context clears the sorted snapshot; you can enable score sorting again. Selecting a moved row still selects the character displayed in that row.

[size=5][b]Compatibility and load order[/b][/size]

[b]Required:[/b] Parley: The Negotiating Table.

[b]Vanilla file replacement:[/b] [b]gui/interaction_marriage.gui[/b]. MCA adds a marriage-specific row, score controls, sorted-list projection and cleanup behavior. It does not replace [b]gui/shared/lists.gui[/b], [b]arrange_marriage_interaction[/b] or [b]marry_off_interaction[/b].

Another mod replacing [b]gui/interaction_marriage.gui[/b] requires a patch preserving both mods' behavior; load order alone cannot merge the files. A mod changing only [b]gui/shared/lists.gui[/b] can work when its row retains the vanilla [b]character_relation[/b] block in the name/age column. This does not certify every list mod.

[b]Vanilla family order:[/b]

[list=1]
[*]Parley: The Negotiating Table
[*]Marriage Calculation Assistant
[/list]

[b]AGOT family order:[/b]

[list=1]
[*]A Game of Thrones
[*]Parley: The Negotiating Table
[*]Marriage Calculation Assistant
[*]AGOT: Marriage Calculation Assistant
[/list]

The checked AGOT combination uses [b]AGOT 0.5.2.1[/b] and [b]AGOT:MCA 2.2.0[/b]. Use the candidate-potential adapter from the 2.2 series with this MCA release; the older 2.1 adapter uses the previous scoring meaning.

[b]Available adapter:[/b] AGOT: Marriage Calculation Assistant. It adds current-dragonrider potential and contains no replacement marriage GUI. No additional interface compatibility patches are included. Enable only one copy of each mod in a playset.

[size=5][b]Saves and tested scope[/b][/size]

Scores are calculated without stamping or modifying candidates. Optional sorting stores a temporary snapshot on the local player, and normal picker cleanup removes it. [b]Close the marriage picker before saving or disabling MCA.[/b] Disabling the mod while a sorting snapshot is still stored can leave inert variables in the save.

The interface has been checked at 100% and 125% UI scale. Other scales, multiplayer and other total conversions are not verified.

Version 3.0.1 restores the AGOT adapter's dragonrider contribution without changing the core weights, sorting or layout.

[size=5][b]Feedback and support[/b][/size]

For a score report, include the candidate, the visible breakdown, picker side, mod versions, load order and a screenshot. For interface problems, also include resolution and UI scale. Distinguish a score that appears wrong from a marriage proposal the AI will not accept: they are separate calculations.

